## Held-out fleets 60-65 (chosen setting only)

| margin | sustain (operating points) | detected | median lead (days) | healthy alarm episodes / turbine-years = per turbine-year (the rule's unit) | per assessable turbine-year | drifting-sensor episodes | pre-onset alarms | assessable share |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1.25 | 18 | 36/36 | 8.9 | 1 / 2.27 = 0.44 | 0.61 | 39 | 1 | 0.59 |

Exposure: 4.53 healthy turbine-years for tuning, 2.27 held out. Zero episodes in 2.27 turbine-years would still allow 1.32 per turbine-year at 95%.

Caveats: the generator and the model share assumptions (KNOWN_LIMITATIONS E3); a slow drift of a single temperature sensor cannot be told apart from heating; these numbers say nothing about real turbines.
